  "nl_text": "The schemabench_0033 database is used to store various components of a web application, specifically related to the Bootstrap 4 framework. It contains 30 tables that represent different types of elements, such as alerts, badges, cards, carousels, collapses, content blocks, grids, jumbotrons, links, list groups, media, pictures, tabs, and utilities. The database is organized around a central table called cms_cmsplugin, which serves as a parent table for all the other tables, referencing their cmsplugin_ptr_id column. This allows for easy management and retrieval of the various components. The cms_cmsplugin table has foreign keys referencing many of the other tables, indicating that these components can be used in various contexts. The database also includes tables for filer_file, filer_image, and filer_thumbmailoption, which are likely used for storing and managing files, images, and thumbnail options, respectively. Each table has a primary key, and some tables have additional constraints, such as unique constraints, composite keys, and foreign keys, which ensure data integrity and relationships between the tables. The database also includes various columns with different data types, such as integers, strings, and long text, which store information about the components, such as their properties, attributes, and relationships.",
  "gold_question": "Background / Context\n\nThe project involves creating a plugin bundle for Django CMS that integrates Bootstrap 4 components. Django CMS Bootstrap 4 Plugin Bundle enables developers to incorporate a variety of Bootstrap 4 components into their Django CMS projects. Bootstrap is a popular front-end framework that provides pre-designed UI components for building responsive web pages.\n\nObjectives\n\nThe primary objective is to provide a set of reusable Bootstrap 4 components that can be easily integrated into Django CMS installations without directly modifying frontend styles or JavaScript.\n\nStakeholders & Users\n\n- Developers: Implement and customize the plugin in their Django CMS projects.\n- CMS Administrators: Utilize the components for creating content without requiring deep technical knowledge.\n\nFunctional Descriptions\n\n1. Component Integration:\n   - Integrate standard Bootstrap 4 components such as Alerts, Badge, Card, Carousel, Collapse, Grid, Jumbotron, Link, List Group, Media, Picture, Tabs, and Utilities.\n\n2. Database Tables:\n   - Maintain component-specific tables each with attributes and foreign keys to manage relations and content efficiently.\n\n3. Alerts:\n   - Configure alerts with context, dismissibility, and tag types.\n\n4. Badge and Card:\n   - Customize badge appearances and card layouts with different contexts and attributes.\n\n5. Carousel:\n   - Manage images and slides within a carousel setup, including controls for interval, indicators, and transitions.\n\n6. Collapse Content:\n   - Manage collapsible content for blockquotes, codes, and figures.\n\n7. Grid Systems:\n   - Utilize Bootstrap’s grid system to define responsive container, row, and column arrangements.\n\n8. Jumbotron:\n   - Configure jumbotron settings with fluid options and attributes.\n\n9. Media and Utilities:\n   - Facilitate media embedding and spacing utilities for layout adjustments.\n\nNon-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Scalability:\n  - Ensure compatibility with existing Django CMS installations and scalability for large content sets.\n  \n- Flexibility:\n  - Allow for the addition of new components without frontend dependencies. Styles and JavaScript must be added manually by the developers as per the project's requirements.\n\n- Usability:\n  - Ensure that CMS administrators can easily use the components through an intuitive interface.\n\n- Performance:\n  - The plugin should not negatively impact the performance of the Django CMS setup.\n\n- Maintainability:\n  - The plugin's codebase should be well-documented and maintainable for adapting to future updates of Django CMS or Bootstrap.",
  "input_json": "/data/SchemaBench/Experiment/schema2text_llama31/0033.json",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0033\nCREATE TABLE `cms_cmsplugin` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cmsplugin_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `plugin_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `created_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `updated_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `cmsplugin_ptr_id_UNIQUE` (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `alerts` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cmsplugin_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `alert_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `message` longtext NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `alerts_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) REFERENCES `cms_cmsplugin` (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `badges` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cmsplugin_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `label` varchar(100) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `badges_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) REFERENCES `cms_cmsplugin` (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `cards` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cmsplugin_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` longtext NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `cards_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) REFERENCES `cms_cmsplugin` (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `carousels` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cmsplugin_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `image_url` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `carousels_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) REFERENCES `cms_cmsplugin` (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `collapses` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cmsplugin_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` longtext NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `collapses_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) REFERENCES `cms_cmsplugin` (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `content_blocks` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cmsplugin_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `content` longtext NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `content_blocks_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) REFERENCES `cms_cmsplugin` (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `grids` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cmsplugin_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `grid_structure` longtext NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `grids_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) REFERENCES `cms_cmsplugin` (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `jumbotrons` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cmsplugin_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `content` longtext NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `jumbotrons_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) REFERENCES `cms_cmsplugin` (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `links` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cmsplugin_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `url` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `text` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `links_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) REFERENCES `cms_cmsplugin` (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `list_groups` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cmsplugin_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `items` longtext NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `list_groups_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) REFERENCES `cms_cmsplugin` (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `media` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cmsplugin_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `media_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `source` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `media_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) REFERENCES `cms_cmsplugin` (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `pictures` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cmsplugin_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `image_url` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `pictures_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) REFERENCES `cms_cmsplugin` (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `tabs` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cmsplugin_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `tab_title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `tab_content` longtext NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `tabs_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) REFERENCES `cms_cmsplugin` (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `utilities` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `cmsplugin_ptr_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `utility_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `utilities_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) REFERENCES `cms_cmsplugin` (`cmsplugin_ptr_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `filer_file` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `file_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `file_path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `filer_image` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `image_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `image_path` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `filer_thumbnailoption` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `option_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `option_value` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
